title: Winter 2025 Cube Drafts
date: 02-01-2026
tags: magic, cube, mtgo

One of my goals for the new year is to write more, but the day job has been a bitter morass where dreams go to die, so we have to stretch our linguistic legs with unexplored topics.

With these seasons of both [the latest MTGO](https://www.mtgo.com/news/tla-vintage-cube-update) and Arena cubes wrapping up, I thought I'd write up some of the decks I drafted.

# 3-0 Grixis Untomb
![Grixis Untomb](/images/blogs/winter-2025-cube-drafts/grixis-untomb.png)

AKA master breacher.

This was a pretty scrungy [Breach](https://scryfall.com/card/thb/161/underworld-breach)/[Brainfreeze](https://scryfall.com/card/scg/29/brain-freeze) deck. The combo's generally played out well in the cube, but with so little card draw, we were mostly just counting on luck here.

[Entombing](https://scryfall.com/card/dmr/82/entomb) for Brainfreeze/LED was actually pretty real. The surprise MVP though was [Master of Death](https://scryfall.com/card/mkc/216/master-of-death), who helped dig while soaking up damage.

As you can see from the sideboard, we bobbed around a bit before settling into the combo (RIP [Ragavan](https://scryfall.com/card/mh2/138/ragavan-nimble-pilferer)). Breach can work as a side plan in an otherwise functional deck, but ours was anemic enough that we had to go all-in on staying alive and Breaching.

# 3-0 Dimir Unicyle
![Dimir Unicycle](/images/blogs/winter-2025-cube-drafts/dimir-unicycle.png)

AKA wheel-less wheel.

The plan here was supposed to be wheeling into card draw punishers, but with only the single [Echo](https://scryfall.com/card/mh1/46/echo-of-eons), that didn't fire off too often. Thankfully, [Sheoldred](https://scryfall.com/card/jmp/278/sheoldred-whispering-one), [Orcish Bowmasters](https://scryfall.com/card/ltr/103/orcish-bowmasters), and [The One Ring](https://scryfall.com/card/ltr/246/the-one-ring) were messed up enough to carry the deck home.

I was kind of waffling on including a [Flash](https://scryfall.com/card/a25/57/flash)/reanmiate package too. Still not sure if it was worth running, but I've been bit by enough awkward reanimator hands that I elected for a more consistent midrange plan.

Just to shout out my last opponent here - they had a super cool lands deck that blew up all of mine. The last game was a real nail-biter and came down to us winning a single turn before they did. Thanks [Doc Oc](https://scryfall.com/card/dsk/42/abhorrent-oculus)!

# 2-1 Lurrus Legends
![Lurrus Legends](/images/blogs/winter-2025-cube-drafts/lurrus-legends.png)

How many drafts have I trainwrecked on [Lurrus](https://scryfall.com/card/iko/226/lurrus-of-the-dream-den)? How many more will I throw away? Alas and alack.

I'm not the first person to point out that [Wan Shi Tong, Librarian](https://scryfall.com/card/tla/78/wan-shi-tong-librarian) is a pretty good Magic card, but it's been awesome for Lurrus decks.

Another one I'll call out here is [Basim Ibn Ishaq](https://scryfall.com/card/acr/49/basim-ibn-ishaq). This is a sore thumb in the cube list, but I will say it performed really well here and I'm curious if I should be taking it higher. Even one trigger's probably enough for him to earn his keep.

# 7-2 Frogwalk
![Frogwalk](/images/blogs/winter-2025-cube-drafts/powered-frogwalk.png)

An absolute pile, but if you slap enough pieces of power together, it'll get the job done.  This deck is the kind of slop I hate, so of course it's the one that went the distance.

The most egregious thing here is [Leovold](https://scryfall.com/card/uma/202/leovold-emissary-of-trest) + [Wheel](https://scryfall.com/card/sum/185/wheel-of-fortune). Even now, after the seven wins, I think it was wrong to play them. If I had to run this back, I'd probably swap for the [Questing Druid](https://scryfall.com/card/woe/234/questing-druid-seek-the-beast) and [Chandra](https://scryfall.com/card/cmm/876/chandra-torch-of-defiance) just to dig deeper to the good stuff.

# 7-1 Naya Fourdrops
![Naya Fourdrops](/images/blogs/winter-2025-cube-drafts/naya-fourdrops.png)

Closed out the season with a winning agro deck.

Between the lack of early plays and some junky fillers (Tireless Tracker, Endurance), I'll admit I'm surprised this deck went the distance. I guess an assertive game plan and a little luck gets the job done.

The curve is definitely heavy, but a mox helps and sticking any of the fours basically wins the game. If I'm in the Boros seat, I'll spec on any green lands in case [Minsc and Boo](https://scryfall.com/card/clb/285/minsc-&-boo-timeless-heroes) show up and they sure delivered.

On the whole, I think [the adjustments to the arena cube](https://www.reddit.com/r/magicTCG/comments/1q4vx8c/arena_powered_cube_20/) were really positive and I'm looking forward to next season!